Good. Before adding more intelligence, we’ll build a **simple real-time debugging dashboard**. In real AI platforms engineers always create **observability tools** to inspect streams and state. Otherwise debugging distributed pipelines becomes very hard.

We’ll build a **lightweight dashboard** using **Streamlit** that shows:

* latest detection events
* latest tracked objects
* active track history in Redis
* detected traffic events

This becomes your **system observability layer**.

---

# 1. Why Dashboards Matter in AI Systems

Production ML systems always include **observability**:

```text
metrics
logs
stream inspection
state inspection
```

Without this you cannot debug:

* dropped frames
* missing events
* tracker failures
* congestion mis-detection

Your dashboard will act as a **stream inspector**.

